{"chunk_id": "9ddb6575d866", "text": "As the war in Lanka intensifies, Indrajita (Meghanada), Ravana\u2019s formidable son, confronts the defector Vibhishana and the allied forces of Rama. Enraged by Vibhishana\u2019s rebukes, Indrajita rides forth in a magnificent chariot drawn by black steeds, appearing like Death itself. Lakshmana, seated upon Hanuman\u2019s back and radiant like the rising sun, steps forward to challenge him. The two exchange fierce taunts: Indrajita boasts of his deadly skill and past victories, while Lakshmana condemns his use of invisibility in battle as the tactic of a rogue. The clash begins as Indrajita releases torrents of arrows that strike Lakshmana like venomous serpents. Though pierced and bloodied, Lakshmana shines with undiminished resolve. The passage highlights the psychological warfare, heroic pride, and mythic scale of this pivotal duel between two supreme warriors.\nLakshmana confronts the furious Indrajita in open battle after fierce taunts, and the two begin a deadly exchange of arrows.\nThemes: heroic combat, war taunts, dharma vs deceit, brotherly loyalty, battlefield valor", "vector": [-0.0046706609427928925, -0.011063162237405777, 0.0011456338688731194, 0.01456107385456562, 0.002543781651183963, 0.005802737083286047, -0.03229467198252678, -0.022112766280770302, -0.03158966824412346, -0.026654629036784172, 0.01568637043237686, 0.004057170823216438, 0.0027844326104968786, -0.005077395122498274, 0.006961928680539131, -0.00386058259755373, 0.04221897944808006, -0.016825225204229355, 0.03725682571530342, -0.012452836148440838, -0.008466844446957111, 0.0028606951236724854, -0.01069710124284029, 0.027956176549196243, -0.032213326543569565, 0.010364935733377934, 0.013964531011879444, -0.02657328173518181, 0.016350703313946724, -0.014981365762650967, -0.008053331635892391, -0.027901945635676384, 0.0016599827213212848, -0.009076944552361965, -0.03473507612943649, -0.008243140764534473, 2.8121836294303648e-05, -0.02340075746178627, 